{
  "schema": "tepna.astgrep-allow/1",
  "README": "Written by hand, read by tools/astgrep-gate.mjs. An entry is keyed by rule, file, the matched TEXT normalised to single spaces, and an ORDINAL among identical triples in the file — never a line number, which moves on every edit above it (the absence-ledger key lesson, #3192). An entry whose hit is gone is a STALE EXEMPTION and reds the gate, so a fix cannot leave its licence behind (DEEP-AUDIT-IV §2, where one file-keyed exemption blinded a whole module to Clock Contract §5).",
  "reasons": {
    "tally": "A count of events, or a duration summed over them. The key is absent exactly when zero were counted, so the default is the measurement and not a gap — §∅ asks whether the device emitted it or our path manufactured it, and a tally manufactures nothing.",
    "presence-test": "The default has only to fail a comparison or a truthiness test; the zero never reaches a published number. `p.get(key, 0) > 0` drops a point that lacks the key, and `mutants_bytes > 0` decides whether a reason mentions a size at all.",
    "invalid-sentinel": "Zero is chosen because it is IMPOSSIBLE for the field, so the consumer refuses: an unknown month name yields month 0, `datetime()` raises ValueError, and the caller leaves `last_sync_utc` absent rather than rolling onto a wrong instant. The comment at the site says so.",
    "config-default": "A configured value whose zero has a stated meaning at the site — `keep_nights` 0 disables retention, `ftype` 0 is the default PMD frame type. A configuration default is not a measurement.",
    "protobuf-absent-is-zero": "Protobuf omits a zero-valued field on the wire, so for the TIME fields of a device-clock read, absent means zero by the format’s own rule. The DATE fields on the same line are read by index and not by `.get`, because a year, month or day of zero is impossible — the asymmetry is the honesty.",
    "canonical-column": "A column index, defaulting to the canonical position of that column in the sidecar the writer emits. Named here because the latent case is real: a sidecar with a renamed header would read column 0 as the stamp rather than report the absence.",
    "rate-table": "`SAMPLE_HZ` holds 0 for PPI deliberately — per-beat events, never back-timed — so zero is already in band in this table. An unknown measurement type cannot reach the back-timing step: `decode_frame` raises on it before `step_ns` is computed.",
    "viewport-default": "A chart viewport bound. It draws an axis and publishes no number, and the maximum side of each pair defaults to 1 and to 50, which is what makes the pair a bound rather than a reading.",
    "counted-zero": "`dawnPhenomenon` omits `nDays` on exactly one path, the early return that fires when no day yielded a dawn window, where the count of qualifying days is genuinely zero — so the default equals the truth. Its sibling `medianRiseMgdl` nulls on that same path because a median over zero days does not exist. Named rather than silent: the early return does not write the field, so a later early return added for a different reason would publish 0 as if days had been examined."
  },
